<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20458] quota: QMT parameter path becomes ambiguous when an OST pool name contains a dot</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20458</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;A pool name containing . injects a spurious level into the lctl parameter hierarchy, so tools like list_param/get_param can no longer tell where the pool name ends and a real sub-parameter begins.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
# lctl list_param qmt.test-QMT0000.*.glb-usr
qmt.test-QMT0000.dt-local.glb-usr           pool &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"local"&lt;/span&gt;        OK
qmt.test-QMT0000.dt-local-1.glb-usr      pool &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"local-1"&lt;/span&gt;     OK
qmt.test-QMT0000.dt-local_1.glb-usr      pool &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"local_1"&lt;/span&gt;     OK
qmt.test-QMT0000.dt-local.abc.glb-usr       pool &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"local.abc"&lt;/span&gt;    BROKEN&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
